# Post-authentication landing & deploy runtime permissions

Canonical rules locked by FIX-LOGIN-REDIRECT-RUNTIME-PERMISSIONS.

## Post-auth redirect
1. Post-auth landing MUST be permission/role-aware via
   `App\Services\Auth\PostAuthenticationRedirectService` — do NOT hardcode
   `redirect()->intended(route('dashboard'))` in auth controllers.
2. `url.intended` MUST NOT override authorization. Honor it only when internal,
   well-formed, route-resolvable, AND authorized for the user (checked against
   the target route's own `permission:`/`role:` middleware).
3. Discard unauthorized / external / protocol-relative / `javascript:` / `data:` /
   malformed / unknown-route intended URLs → fall back to the role-aware default.
4. Preserve authorized intended URLs (e.g. `/profile`, `/lab/v2-orders` for Admin Lab).
5. Admin Lab is Lab-only: default landing = `lab-v2-orders.index`; `/dashboard` stays 403.
6. NEVER fix a redirect 403 by granting a role dashboard permission or Super Admin.
7. All auth completion paths (login, registration, email verification, password
   confirmation, online-context) use the same resolver.
8. Keep session regeneration; consume intended on use; no redirect loop.

## Deploy runtime permissions (`scripts/deploy-vps.sh`)
9.  Laravel runtime dirs (`storage/**`, `bootstrap/cache`) MUST be owned by and
    writable to the PHP-FPM runtime user after deploy. Fail closed if it resolves to root.
10. Cache artisan commands (`optimize:clear`/`config:cache`/`route:cache`/`view:cache`/
    `event:cache`) run as the runtime user (`runuser`), never as root.
11. No world-writable (0777) mode. Use `2775` dirs (setgid) + `0664` files. Ownership
    normalized after ALL artisan/smoke commands.
12. Mandatory writable gates (CACHE/SESSION/VIEW CACHE/LOG/BOOTSTRAP CACHE WRITE) — one
    FAIL aborts the deploy (NOT GO).
13. Deploy MUST run the authenticated authorization smoke
    (`deploy:auth-landing-smoke --strict`) — guest smoke alone is insufficient; it must
    exercise the Spatie permission-cache path. NO_GO if authenticated landing 500/403.
14. `deploy-vps-runner.sh` runs ON the VPS, not locally. Backup-first; `migrate --force`
    only; no `migrate:fresh`/`db:wipe`; no secret/PII in logs.
